@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About Ticks";
}

<div class="about-ticks">
    <h1>About Ticks</h1>

    <p>
        Ticks are small relatives of spiders that feed on the blood
        of animals, including people. They attach when a person or
        animal brushes past vegetation, they do not jump or fly.
        They can be found in woodland, grassland, parks and gardens.
    </p>

    <nav class="about-links" aria-label="On this page">
        <a href="#tick-species">Tick species</a>
        <a href="#bite-prevention">Tick bite prevention</a>
        <a href="#seasonal-activity">Seasonal tick activity</a>
    </nav>

    <section id="tick-species" class="about-section">
        <h2>Tick species</h2>

        <p>
            The UK is home to several tick species.
            Some examples are described below.
        </p>

        <article class="species-entry">
            <h3>Sheep or deer tick</h3>
            <p class="species-latin"><em>Ixodes ricinus</em></p>
            <p>
                The UK's most widespread tick species. It feeds on wild
                animals, domestic animals and people, and can transmit
                the bacteria responsible for Lyme disease.
            </p>
            <img src="~/images/ticks/ixodes-ricinus.jpg"
                 alt="Sheep or deer tick (Ixodes ricinus)"
                 class="species-image"
                 loading="lazy" />
            <p></p>
        </article>

        <article class="species-entry">
            <h3>Hedgehog tick</h3>
            <p class="species-latin"><em>Ixodes hexagonus</em></p>
            <p>
                Commonly associated with hedgehogs. It also feeds on
                companion animals and can bite people.
            </p>
            <img src="~/images/ticks/ixodes-hexagonus.jpg"
                 alt="Hedgehog tick (Ixodes hexagonus)"
                 class="species-image"
                 loading="lazy" />
            <p></p>
        </article>

        <article class="species-entry">
            <h3>Fox or badger tick</h3>
            <p class="species-latin"><em>Ixodes canisuga</em></p>
            <p>
                Found widely across the UK, this species commonly
                feeds on foxes, badgers and domestic dogs.
            </p>
            <img src="~/images/ticks/ixodes-canisuga.jpg"
                 alt="Fox or badger tick (Ixodes canisuga)"
                 class="species-image"
                 loading="lazy" />
            <p></p>
        </article>

        <article class="species-entry">
            <h3>Ornate cow tick</h3>
            <p class="species-latin"><em>Dermacentor reticulatus</em></p>
            <p>
                Mainly recorded in Wales and south-west England,
                with an established population also reported in Essex.
                Its patterned back is a distinctive feature.
            </p>
            <img src="~/images/ticks/dermacentor-reticulatus.jpg"
                 alt="Ornate cow tick (Dermacentor reticulatus)"
                 class="species-image"
                 loading="lazy" />
            <p></p>
        </article>

        <article class="species-entry">
            <h3>Red sheep tick</h3>
            <p class="species-latin"><em>Haemaphysalis punctata</em></p>
            <p>
                Mainly found in south-east England, with records also
                from south Wales. It commonly feeds on sheep,
                although it can also bite people.
            </p>
            <img src="~/images/ticks/haemaphysalis-punctata.jpeg"
                 alt="Red sheep tick (Haemaphysalis punctata)"
                 class="species-image"
                 loading="lazy" />
            <p></p>
        </article>

        <article class="species-entry">
            <h3>Seabird tick</h3>
            <p class="species-latin"><em>Ixodes uriae</em></p>
            <p>
                Associated with seabirds around the UK coast,
                from Shetland to Cornwall. It can also feed on people.
            </p>
            <img src="~/images/ticks/ixodes-uriae.jpg"
                 alt="Seabird tick (Ixodes uriae)"
                 class="species-image"
                 loading="lazy" />
            <p></p>
        </article>

        <p>
            Unsure which species you spotted? Enter “Unknown” when
            reporting. These examples are not a complete identification guide.
        </p>

        <p>
            Source:
            <a href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tick-species-profiles">
                UKHSA tick species profiles
            </a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="bite-prevention" class="about-section">
        <h2>Tick bite prevention</h2>

        <p>
            A few precautions can help reduce the chance of a bite
            when spending time outdoors:
        </p>

        <ul class="prevention-list">
            <li>
                Wear clothing that covers your skin and tuck
                trousers into socks.
            </li>
            <li>
                Choose light clothing to make crawling ticks
                easier to notice.
            </li>
            <li>
                Keep to clear paths where possible.
            </li>
            <li>
                Use an appropriate insect repellent, following
                its instructions.
            </li>
            <li>
                Check your skin and clothing after outdoor activities.
                Check children and pets too.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>If you find an attached tick</h3>

        <p>
            Remove it promptly. With fine-tipped tweezers,
            grip close to the skin and pull slowly upwards,
            avoiding squeezing its body.
            Afterwards, wash the area with soap and water
            or use antiseptic.
        </p>

        <p>
            If you develop a spreading rash or feel unwell after
            a tick bite or possible exposure, contact your GP
            and mention the exposure.
        </p>

        <p>
            Read the
            <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/lyme-disease/">
                NHS guidance on Lyme disease and tick removal
            </a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section id="seasonal-activity" class="about-section">
        <h2>Seasonal tick activity</h2>

        <p>
            View monthly reported sightings for a city and year.
            These educational records do not measure tick populations
            or the risk of being bitten.
        </p>

        <div class="chart-filters">
            <div>
                <label for="chartCity" class="form-label">City</label>
                <select id="chartCity" class="form-select" disabled></select>
            </div>

            <div>
                <label for="chartYear" class="form-label">Year</label>
                <select id="chartYear" class="form-select" disabled></select>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p id="chartStatus" role="status">Loading sightings…</p>

        <div id="seasonalChart" hidden>
            <h3 id="chartTitle"></h3>

            <table class="activity-chart">
                <caption class="visually-hidden">
                    Monthly reported tick sighting totals
                </caption>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Month</th>
                        <th scope="col">Reported sightings</th>
                        <th scope="col">Total</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody id="chartRows"></tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <p class="text-muted mt-3">
            Source: Elanco student task API.
        </p>
    </section>
</div>

@section Scripts {
    <script>
        document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", async function () {
            const citySelect = document.getElementById("chartCity");
            const yearSelect = document.getElementById("chartYear");
            const status = document.getElementById("chartStatus");
            const chart = document.getElementById("seasonalChart");
            const title = document.getElementById("chartTitle");
            const rows = document.getElementById("chartRows");

            const months = [
                "January", "February", "March", "April",
                "May", "June", "July", "August",
                "September", "October", "November", "December"
            ];

            let sightings = [];

            function updateChart() {
                const city = citySelect.value;
                const year = Number(yearSelect.value);
                const totals = new Array(12).fill(0);

                sightings.forEach(function (sighting) {
                    if (sighting.location === city &&
                        sighting.year === year) {
                        totals[sighting.month - 1]++;
                    }
                });

                const maximum = Math.max(...totals, 1);
                const total = totals.reduce((sum, count) => sum + count, 0);

                title.textContent =
                    "Reported tick sightings — " + city + ", " + year;

                rows.replaceChildren();

                months.forEach(function (month, index) {
                    const row = document.createElement("tr");

                    const label = document.createElement("th");
                    label.scope = "row";
                    label.textContent = month;

                    const barCell = document.createElement("td");
                    const track = document.createElement("div");
                    track.className = "activity-track";
                    track.setAttribute("aria-hidden", "true");

                    const bar = document.createElement("div");
                    bar.className = "activity-bar";
                    bar.style.width =
                        (totals[index] / maximum * 100) + "%";

                    track.appendChild(bar);
                    barCell.appendChild(track);

                    const count = document.createElement("td");
                    count.textContent = totals[index];

                    row.append(label, barCell, count);
                    rows.appendChild(row);
                });

                status.textContent = total === 0
                    ? "No sightings reported for this city and year."
                    : total + " sightings reported for this city and year.";

                chart.hidden = false;
            }

            try {
                const response = await fetch(
                    '@Url.Action("Data", "Sightings")'
                );

                if (response.status === 429) {
                    throw new Error(
                        "Too many requests. Please wait a minute and reload."
                    );
                }

                if (!response.ok) {
                    throw new Error(
                        "Sightings could not be loaded. Please try again later."
                    );
                }

                const result = await response.json();
                const data = result.sightings;

                if (!Array.isArray(data)) {
                    throw new Error("The API returned an unexpected response.");
                }

                sightings = data.flatMap(function (item) {
                    const match = typeof item.date === "string"
                        ? item.date.match(/^(\d{4})-(\d{2})-(\d{2})/)
                        : null;

                    if (!match ||
                        typeof item.location !== "string" ||
                        !item.location.trim()) {
                        return [];
                    }

                    const month = Number(match[2]);

                    if (month < 1 || month > 12) {
                        return [];
                    }

                    return [{
                        location: item.location,
                        year: Number(match[1]),
                        month: month
                    }];
                });

                if (sightings.length === 0) {
                    status.textContent = "No sightings are currently available.";
                    return;
                }

                const cities = [...new Set(
                    sightings.map(item => item.location)
                )].sort();

                const years = [...new Set(
                    sightings.map(item => item.year)
                )].sort((a, b) => b - a);

                cities.forEach(function (city) {
                    citySelect.add(new Option(city, city));
                });

                years.forEach(function (year) {
                    yearSelect.add(new Option(year, year));
                });

                if (cities.includes("London")) {
                    citySelect.value = "London";
                }

                citySelect.disabled = false;
                yearSelect.disabled = false;

                citySelect.addEventListener("change", updateChart);
                yearSelect.addEventListener("change", updateChart);

                updateChart();
            }
            catch (error) {
                status.textContent = error instanceof TypeError
                    ? "Unable to connect to the sightings API. Please try again later."
                    : error.message;
            }
        });
    </script>
}